(text "TS06-DRV  ·  Backlight"
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 12.7 0)
(effects
(font
(size 3 3)
(bold yes)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "6e268369-a1c8-5d0e-9cc4-cb58d78d0b3b")
)
(text "Eight amber LEDs behind the tubes are each sourced from their own MCP23017 port-B pin through an isolated 8 x 220R network; the 'm' LED of AM/PM runs\nfrom D12 through 220R. All nine cathodes share BL_K behind one MPSA42, so D11's PWM sets the brightness of them all."
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 19.05 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.524 1.524)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "00befeb8-387b-5129-8a9e-6dea3dac97ab")
)
(text "On the display board: BL_A1..BL_A8 feed the anodes of HL1..HL8, M_A the anode of HL9 (the 'm'),\nand BL_K is all nine cathodes. GPBk of U3 lights HL(k+1): tools/ts06pair.py BL_OF_GPB."
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 40.64 78.74 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.27 1.27)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "add9f442-a41a-583d-bf26-cbebfc59621a")
)
(text "Notes from tools/ts06pair.py"
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 90.17 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.524 1.524)
(bold yes)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "a257cfb5-f2bb-5869-aa95-8f7e513d1254")
)
(text "R53: The m LED, from D12. Standing: one of the four series resistors where the Nano's corridor lines end and change face (tools/mkpcb_drv.py).\nRN1: Isolated resistor network, 8 x 220R (4116R-1-221 class): GPBk -> pin 8-k, resistor to pin 9+k -> its LED.\nVT20: Common-cathode switch for all nine LEDs: D11's PWM is the brightness."
(exclude_from_sim no)
(at 20.32 92.71 0)
(effects
(font
(size 1.27 1.27)
)
(justify left top)
)
(uuid "162bfbc8-8389-5e0b-972d-e72434a171b7")
)
